<ArticleLayout
  title="GarageCloud vs TechMan | Comparison"
  description="How GarageCloud compares to TechMan: pricing, contract terms and who each is built for. TechMan is the UK's most established garage system; GarageCloud is a newer, lower-cost alternative."
  eyebrow="Comparison"
  breadcrumbLabel="GarageCloud vs TechMan"
  heading="GarageCloud vs TechMan"
  lede="TechMan is the most established garage management system in the UK. GarageCloud is a newer, lower-cost alternative without a long contract."
>
  <p>
    <strong>TechMan is a genuinely well-established system</strong> — a UK-built, cloud-based platform with over
    14,500 active users and more than 15 years in the market, according to
    <a href="https://www.capterra.co.uk/software/172835/techman" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Capterra's TechMan listing</a>.
    For a lot of UK workshops, it has been the default choice for a long time.
  </p>

  <h2>Pricing and contract length</h2>
  <p>
    TechMan publishes three tiers — Lite at £189/month, Advanced at £315/month and Pro at £415/month — tied to a
    3-year contract. GarageCloud's Starter plan is £50/month excluding VAT, with no multi-year commitment.
  </p>

  <h2>What TechMan does well</h2>
  <p>
    TechMan's digital vehicle health check includes customer-facing video and photo, and it integrates directly with
    Autodata for labour times and technical data — a genuinely deep feature set built specifically for service and
    repair workshops over a long product history, with multi-location support for groups running more than one
    site.
  </p>

  <h2>What to weigh up</h2>
  <p>
    The 3-year contract and the step up in price between tiers (£189 to £415/month) is a meaningful commitment for a
    smaller or newer workshop. GarageCloud's flat £50–£150/month range and month-to-month structure is aimed at
    workshops that want to try a system without locking in for three years.
  </p>

  <h2>Where GarageCloud is different, not necessarily better</h2>
  <p>
    GarageCloud is pre-launch and does not have TechMan's 15-year track record or its Autodata integration yet. A
    workshop that specifically needs Autodata-integrated VHC today has a real reason to choose TechMan. A workshop
    that wants to start smaller, without a long contract, is the workshop GarageCloud is built for.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
